  "patch_application": "git apply --unidiff-zero",
  "hypothesis": "7228/7229 locate32.8B sampled periods in GC under Reduce/sparse collection,23.8-24.0B self, including repeated logical-position/garbage predicates and a second watch-forward walk. Mark unretained old records INVALID_REF in the existing retention pass; retained records receive packed Refs. Logical prefix is packed contiguously, so forwarded Ref below packed prefix boundary exactly identifies retained prefix watches. Stable fused filter/forward uses no global array or new allocation. Whole-arena/dense paths unchanged. Independent retained7144 base; normal telemetry and all scheduling/tick/proof contracts retained.",
  "test_consideration": "26240 fused versus old two-pass watch states compare every live word, layout and hole count, including duplicates, mixed order, empty lists, mapped Ref0 and subsequent appends.896 actual collector states compare retained7144 and candidate arena/live-watch/layout/occurrence/eager/OTFS digests across seven cuts,16 garbage masks, aliases, physical dense mode and register preservation. Full Release/BC/trace suites and focused kernel/root-lock/retry tests cover protected reasons and roots. Independent proofs/models, twice-run sanitizers, BC, complete GC/Reduce and repeated runtime/RSS remain required; deterministic states are not fuzz acceptance.",
  "risk": "Prefix garbage is intentionally retained unless its aliased source is excluded. Every uncopied record must have INVALID_REF before watch filtering; small stale searched cursors must not masquerade as prefix references. Retained replacement cursors, blockers, order and reason/eager/OTFS forwarding must remain exact. Dead watch spare words need not match but live layout and later append behavior must. Sentinel writes may cost more than removed lookups; complete GC/Reduce and whole-runtime/RSS decide. No N1/API/guard/proof vocabulary changes.",
  "status": "Isolated unfuzzed investigation; retained7144 rollback. No production promotion, changed scheduling, fuzz waiver, old-pin mutation or acceptance before tests and matched performance evidence.",
